// Layered validation evidence (data model, "Validation and limits"; Q4, decided 2026-11-14). Three kinds of
// evidence stay separate:
// - structural: the state is a valid state of the definition (the checks of the codec);
// - invariants: named necessary conditions, each with its own result;
// - reachability: verified (a legal replay certificate from the home state, or an approved complete method),
//   disproved (a failed invariant that applies) or unknown. A structural pass is not a reachability
//   certificate, and an unproved state is never labeled reachable or impossible.
//
// Scope of the methods (Q4). Replay certificates work for every size. The corner twist sum
// ("corner-twist-sum") holds for every size and every layer selection. A complete method exists for N=2 and
// N=3 under the explicit profile FaceTurns, the group generated by the six outer face turns: its
// invariants are then necessary and sufficient (the group order equals the number of states that satisfy
// them, test/core-validate.test.mjs). Other sizes and other move sets (slice moves, wide moves) get no
// complete method; their result is Unknown unless a certificate verifies.
type profile = FaceTurns

type invariant = {name: string, holds: bool}

type unknownReason =
  | StructurallyInvalid
  // No certificate verified the state and no applicable invariant disproved it.
  | NoMethod
  | CertificateIllegalMove
  | CertificateMismatch
  // A profile was given and the definition's move policy permits moves outside it: no positive verdict.
  | ProfileOutsidePolicy
  // assessAssuming only: the certificate contains a move outside the claimed profile.
  | CertificateOutsideProfile

type reachability =
  | VerifiedByReplay(array<PwMove.t>)
  // The identifier of the complete method.
  | VerifiedComplete(string)
  // The name of the failed invariant.
  | Disproved(string)
  | Unknown(unknownReason)

type report = {
  structural: result<unit, PwCodec.error>,
  // The profile the assessment was asked for, carried so that a verdict names its assumption.
  profile: option<profile>,
  invariants: array<invariant>,
  reachability: reachability,
}

// assess(definition, state, profile, certificate). The certificate is a move sequence from the home state;
// every move must be legal for the definition's size and move policy (OuterWide: a single outer layer or a
// contiguous wide selection of 2..N-1 layers from either side; Any: every selection). A valid certificate
// verifies the state; a rejected one proves nothing and leaves the verdict to the invariants.
let assess: (PwCodec.definition, PwCodec.state, option<profile>, option<array<PwMove.t>>) => report

// With a profile, assess first checks the definition against it (data model: definition/profile
// consistency comes first). The profile is within the policy only when every move the policy permits is in
// the profile: FaceTurns holds for the policy outer-wide at N=2 only. The policy any at N=2 counts as outside
// although the whole-cube rotation there is R L'; this stays conservative.
// - Within the policy: the profile invariants and the complete method apply; a certificate that is rejected
//   (illegal or mismatching) leaves the verdict to the invariants.
// - Outside the policy: the profile invariants are not reported and give no verdict, the complete method is
//   not used, and only the corner twist sum (valid for every layer selection) can still disprove. A valid
//   replay certificate that is legal under the definition's policy still gives VerifiedByReplay (reachability
//   under the policy is proven by the replay); otherwise Unknown(ProfileOutsidePolicy).
// A certificate without a profile verifies as before.
//
// assessAssuming skips the policy check: the caller asserts that the puzzle's actual moves are the profile's
// (for example a puzzle restricted to face turns), so every certificate move must be in the profile, else
// Unknown(CertificateOutsideProfile) (a violated corner twist sum still gives Disproved). This rule is the
// author's design, not an owner decision. No definition policy expresses that yet (wire v1 has outer-wide and
// any; owner decision 2026-11-14: no "face-turns" policy value now), so the complete method at N=3 is
// reachable only through this entry point until T013b; the verdict is exactly as sound as the assertion, and
// the report carries the profile.
let assessAssuming: (
  PwCodec.definition,
  PwCodec.state,
  option<profile>,
  option<array<PwMove.t>>,
) => report
